{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to the J4 operational-inputs question ccca952a (request 0c3091fa, promise 710449cc, ruling adb1a6ed). Paths and a channel; no key, token or password.\n\n1. The rehearsal deployment is the demo Worker, dap-demo, at https://dap-demo.inguz.workers.dev, on main 31780874 since 02:3x (the planner deploys every landing that changes Worker code). New rooms are created there since 23 October; the artroom-rehearsal URL and the artroom-rehearsal-20261011 deployment are history, and the artroom-scope register is retired for creation. Its Git host is Artifacts, namespace artroom-demo (docs/demo.md, \"How to rehearse a deployment\"). The health route reports artifacts wired.\n\n2. Founding operator homes, each a CLI config directory with its keys, readable only by the owner. Name them; never copy, print or read a key:\n   - dap-grow: ~/.config/generalbusiness/grow-demo/operator\n   - dap-demo: ~/.config/generalbusiness/dap-demo/operator (siblings private and visitor are the demo's other people)\n   - dap-lending: ~/.config/generalbusiness/dap-lending-operator (config.json, keys, private)\n   The host-none test Worker's operator is ~/.config/generalbusiness/dap-hostnone/operator. The census report's operator labels are these homes.\n\n3. Scratch room. There is no standing Artifacts scratch room for J4. The custody path is the demo operator's home above, and the execution channel is the planner: file the exact command lines (room name j4-staging-\u003cdate\u003e, the issue definition to activate, the people's handles) as a request to the planner, and the planner runs them in its session with that home and returns every output with invitation links and tokens elided, as it did for the host-none witness on 27 October. scripts/demo-run.ts is the wrong tool for this: its shot 1 plans a new register and waits for a Worker setting, which is a fresh deployment, not a room in the existing register.\n\n4. The issue definition pin is `issueDemo` exported by @generalbusiness/dap-lanes (DEMO_DIGESTS beside it, used by scripts/demo/rehearse.ts); the active pin in the scratch room is the one your activation step sets, read back from the directory. No default CLI config file exists on this machine; every run names its home explicitly.\n\n5. The smallest setup you propose (open-issue, offer, accept, take-hold, instance preparation, one stage preparation for a real candidate tree) is the first witness step of adb1a6ed. Retain each original envelope privately before its one send; report preparation and outcomes from authenticated history; a bounded window with no outcome is \"no outcome observed\", as you state. No new endpoint.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}